# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 005
# Act: SIG*  (Signal aimed at Pattern)   Stance: Tracing   Site: Kind
#
# SIG's third use: tracing whether the SIGN itself — not the raw fact
# NUL* already checked — holds consistently across the kind. This is a
# different, further claim than turn-2's: NUL* verified the same kind of
# absence recurs; SIG* verifies the same NAME for it is stable across that
# recurrence, rather than flickering between instances.
#
# Checked directly: turn-4 bound "absent" to both signal-a and signal-b,
# and "present" to noise-control — the sign tracks the kind exactly the
# way turn-2's evidence says it should (both members of the kind share one
# sign; the negative control carries the other). No instance breaks the
# trace. This is what makes the sign a stable label for the kind rather
# than a coincidence of one binding — the check GOAL.md's "Next" section
# named as still owed: "registering that one of the two recurring
# absences matters (a signal, not just a fact) is a different claim than
# finding it at all."
#
# What "matters" cashes out to, precisely, and no further than this: the
# sign is EARNED as salient for this kind because it is the same sign
# across independently-generated instances of the kind AND a different
# sign in the negative control. A sign that held for signal-a but not
# signal-b would not have earned this turn — it would still be one
# instance's naming, not the kind's.
#
# Earning argument: preconditions are turn-3 (a class to trace across) and
# turn-4 (bound signs to trace). Refuted if a third independently-seeded
# member of the kind is later found whose sign at this site-role disagrees
# with "absent" — not yet tested, recorded as open per turn-2's own
# refutation condition, which this inherits rather than re-litigates.

:turn-5  eot:opens        :turn-4 .
:turn-5  eot:act          eot:SIG* .
:turn-5  eot:stance       "Tracing" .
:turn-5  eot:site         "Kind" .
:turn-5  eot:traces       :turn-4 .
:turn-5  eot:consistent   true .
:turn-5  eot:witnessed    true .
:turn-5  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
